{
  "Logging": {
    "LogLevel": {
      "Default": "Information",
      "Microsoft.AspNetCore": "Warning",
      // Every stage of a call, so a slow or looping call can be read off the log directly
      // rather than reproduced. Turn back to Information once the pipeline settles.
      "Secretary.Agents": "Debug",
      "Secretary.Api.Voice": "Debug",
      // Every inbound Gemini message, one line each. The only way to see where a slow turn
      // actually spends its time — turn boundaries alone pointed at the wrong culprit twice.
      "Secretary.Voice.Google": "Debug"
    },
    "Console": {
      // Without this the console writes no times at all, which makes "it answers every ten
      // seconds" impossible to check against the log.
      "TimestampFormat": "HH:mm:ss.fff ",
      "UseUtcTimestamp": false
    }
  },
  "AllowedHosts": "*",
  "Cors": {
    "AllowedOrigins": ["http://localhost:5173"]
  },
  "ConnectionStrings": {
    // Windows auth, so there is no credential here to keep out of the repo. Its own database,
    // deliberately not the old solution's ai_assist — the two run side by side.
    // PostgreSQL at production deploy:
    //   Host=...;Port=5432;Database=secretary;Username=...;Password=...  (user-secrets)
    "Default": "Server=localhost;Database=secretary;Trusted_Connection=True;MultipleActiveResultSets=true;TrustServerCertificate=True"
  },
  "Jwt": {
    "Issuer": "Secretary",
    "Audience": "Secretary.Clients",
    "SigningKey": "set-via-user-secrets-or-environment-variable-never-committed",
    "ExpiryMinutes": 480
  },
  "AgentProviders": {
    "OpenAi": {
      "ApiKey": "set-via-user-secrets-or-environment-variable-never-committed",
      "Model": "gpt-5.6"
    }
  },
  "OpenAiRealtime": {
    "ApiKey": "set-via-user-secrets-or-environment-variable-never-committed",
    "Model": "gpt-realtime-2.1",
    "AudioFormat": "pcm16",
    "SampleRateHz": 24000
  },
  "GeminiLive": {
    // AiStudio for local work (an API key and nothing else); Enterprise — the platform that
    // used to be Vertex AI — for production, where quotas and SLA are real. The SDK takes both
    // from the same client, so nothing downstream changes.
    "Backend": "AiStudio",
    "ApiKey": "set-via-user-secrets-or-environment-variable-never-committed",
    "Project": "",
    "Location": "europe-west3",
    "Model": "gemini-3.1-flash-live-preview",
    // A prebuilt Gemini voice. Which one carries Azerbaijani acceptably is a real-call question.
    "Voice": "Aoede",
    "LanguageCode": "az-AZ",
    "MaxOutputTokens": 1200,
    // How long the caller goes quiet before Gemini treats the turn as over. Lower is snappier;
    // too low and it talks over someone drawing breath mid-sentence. Tune from real calls.
    "EndOfSpeechSilenceMs": 500,
    // True on measured evidence: a 200 ms "xeyr" took Gemini 7.3 s to report, against ~1.5 s
    // for a two-second sentence in the same call. Set false if false barge-ins appear.
    "EagerStartOfSpeech": true,
    "PrefixPaddingMs": 300,
    // Experiment: transcription is the last thing we put on the critical path, and the caller's
    // transcript and the model's first audio always arrive together. Turn back on if it does not
    // visibly help — the transcript is what makes a call reviewable.
    "TranscribeCaller": false,
    // Zero disables thinking. A caller hears deliberation as dead air, and a receptionist has
    // nothing to deliberate about. Raise it only if the agent makes poor choices, not slow ones.
    "ThinkingBudgetTokens": 0
  },
  "ModelPricing": {
    "_comment": [
      "USD per 1,000,000 tokens unless a per-minute rate is given. Editing these affects FUTURE",
      "calls only — each call's cost is worked out once and stored on the call record, so history",
      "never moves when a rate is corrected.",
      "",
      "The API refuses to start if the realtime model OR any of the three VoiceV2:OpenAi models",
      "has no entry here — an unpriced model records every call it serves as free.",
      "",
      "Provenance, because not all of these are equally certain:",
      "  gpt-realtime-2.1, -mini, gpt-5.6  OpenAI pricing page, 2026-07-27.",
      "  gpt-4o-mini-tts                   supplied directly; not on the public page.",
      "  gpt-4o(-mini)-transcribe          the page gives ONE input rate; it is applied here to",
      "                                    both text and audio input. If those are billed",
      "                                    separately, these two are wrong.",
      "  whisper-1                         long-published $0.006/min, not re-checked 2026-07-27.",
      "  gpt-5.6                           may have tiers (Sol/Terra/Luna at $5/$2.50/$1); $5.00",
      "                                    assumes Sol. Wrong tier means a 5x error.",
      "",
      "The check that settles all of it: compare a month of recorded CostUsd against the OpenAI",
      "invoice. Token counts come from the provider, so any gap is a rate, and the Dashboard's",
      "per-pipeline breakdown says which model it belongs to."
    ],
    "Models": {
      "gpt-realtime-2.1": {
        "TextInputPerMillionUsd": 4.00,
        "CachedTextInputPerMillionUsd": 0.40,
        "TextOutputPerMillionUsd": 24.00,
        "AudioInputPerMillionUsd": 32.00,
        "CachedAudioInputPerMillionUsd": 0.40,
        "AudioOutputPerMillionUsd": 64.00
      },
      // Billed by audio duration, not tokens — it reports no token counts at all, so without
      // this rate every call it serves would be recorded as free. Still used for the realtime
      // path's input transcription.
      "whisper-1": {
        "PerAudioMinuteUsd": 0.006
      },
      "gpt-5.6": {
        "TextInputPerMillionUsd": 5.00,
        "CachedTextInputPerMillionUsd": 0.50,
        "TextOutputPerMillionUsd": 30.00
      },
      // ⚠ These are the published Gemini 2.5 Flash native-audio rates, applied to 3.1 Flash
      // Live because per-token rates for 3.1 were not published at the time of writing — only
      // per-minute figures. Roughly a quarter of gpt-realtime either way, which is the whole
      // reason for trying it, but treat a Gemini call's recorded cost as indicative until it is
      // checked against a real Google invoice.
      "gemini-3.1-flash-live-preview": {
        "TextInputPerMillionUsd": 0.50,
        "AudioInputPerMillionUsd": 3.00,
        "AudioOutputPerMillionUsd": 12.00
      }
    }
  }
}
